        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: South Cheshire Way, Cheshire, England, Grindley Brook, Whitchurch, Mow Cop, Staffordshire, North West, West Midlands\n- Topics: long-distance footpaths, route sections, regional boundaries\n\nFacts:\n- The South Cheshire Way is a 32 mi long-distance footpath in England.\n- The South Cheshire Way runs east-west mainly through Cheshire.\n- The western section of the South Cheshire Way starts from Grindley Brook near Whitchurch and runs through farmland.\n- The eastern section of the South Cheshire Way starts from the isolated village of Mow Cop.\n- The eastern section of the South Cheshire Way straddles the Cheshire-Staffordshire border.\n- The eastern section of the South Cheshire Way is divided between the North West and West Midlands regions of England.",
